-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing below is bundled in the Provael sdist or wheel. The optional extras declared in
pyproject.toml install these packages from their own distributions under their own licences;
they are listed here because a Provael run that uses them produces results the project publishes.

  lerobot (Hugging Face)                Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot
    Installed by the [lerobot] and [hardware] extras (pinned 0.5.1). Provides the SmolVLA policy
    loading path and the LIBERO simulator environment.

  LIBERO (Lifelong Robot Learning)      MIT License
    https://github.com/Lifelong-Robot-Learning/LIBERO
    Installed through lerobot's [libero] extra. The benchmark the published body was measured on.

  openpi-client (Physical Intelligence) Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi
    Installed by the [openpi] extra. Websocket client to an openpi policy server.

One third-party file is checked into this repository outside the Python package:

  paper/spais/neurips_2026.sty          NeurIPS 2026 LaTeX style file, used under its authors'
                                        terms for a conference submission; not part of any
                                        distributed Provael artifact.

No MuJoCo Menagerie or other simulator asset is vendored in this repository.
